                    </div>
                    <div class="filter-search-actions">
                        <p>Literal text and UTC bounds apply only to retained search. Progress and result controls appear above the event list.</p>
                        <button id="search-start" data-help-key="logs.search-start" type="button" class="btn btn-outline-primary" onclick="startSearch()">Search retained files</button>
                    </div>
                </form>
                        <div class="filter-diagnostics">
                            <label class="diagnostic-control"><input type="checkbox" id="diagnosticsSwitch" onchange="setDiagnosticVisibility(this.checked)" data-help-key="logs.diagnostics" data-help-proxy> Diagnostics</label>
                            <p>Show sandbox UI activity and supporting diagnostic events. Real call-flow and protocol events stay visible when hidden.</p>
                        </div>
                    </section>
                    <section id="workbench-panel-coverage" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="workbench-tab-coverage" data-panel="coverage" class="workbench-section" hidden onclick="coverageAction(event)"><h2>Sources and evidence</h2>
                        <p id="source-summary" data-help-key="logs.coverage-sources"><strong>Sources in this evidence scope: loading…</strong></p>
                        <p>An available log stream means readable retained files; it does not prove every event or hop was recorded.</p>
                        <h3>Loaded evidence and limits</h3>
                        <p id="coverage-warning" role="status" data-help-key="logs.coverage-warning"></p>
                        <p id="page-coverage" data-help-key="logs.coverage-evidence">Loading evidence coverage…</p>
                        <p>Trace spans cover actual gateway requests and internal auth subrequests, shared Node server middleware, adapter → PCM attempts and adapter → native HAPI calls. HAPI runtime records include request, permission and selected native error observations; HAPI import remains a separate source. Recorded parent IDs show observed causality; a parent or child may be outside these retained results. Caller-supplied trace IDs are hints, not verified identities. Cache hits and direct calls can skip hops. Filtering cannot add missing instrumentation or dropped records.</p>
                        <details open><summary data-help-key="logs.coverage-filter">Find events by source, role or HO</summary>
                            <p>Buttons apply one exact filter and keep other filters and Diagnostics. Remove a filter below or use browser Back to restore the previous view.</p><ul id="source-list" class="journey-list"></ul>
                        </details>
                        <div id="coverage-active-filters" role="group" aria-label="Remove coverage filters"></div>
                        <details><summary data-help-key="logs.coverage-health">Later source checks</summary><p id="source-latest-check"></p></details>
                        <details><summary id="journey-summary" data-help-key="logs.coverage-journey">Observed ID groups in the loaded page: loading…</summary><p>Each recorded Flow, Trace and Correlation ID is counted separately; groups may share rows. Inspect an exact ID across roles and organizations: other filters are explicitly set aside, Diagnostics is preserved, and Return restores the prior view. Results show recorded evidence, not complete traces or causality.</p><ul id="journey-list" class="journey-list"></ul></details>
                        <details><summary data-help-key="logs.coverage-legend">Role color legend</summary><p>Color key only; these roles are not all necessarily configured or observed.</p>
                <div class="role-legend" aria-label="Component role color legend">
                    <span class="badge role-badge role-pcm">PCM</span>
                    <span class="badge role-badge role-doctor">Doctor</span>
                    <span class="badge role-badge role-gateway">Gateway</span>
                    <span class="badge role-badge role-adapter">Adapter</span>
                    <span class="badge role-badge role-hapi" data-help-key="logs.role-hapi-runtime">HAPI runtime</span>
                    <span class="badge role-badge role-hapi-import">HAPI import only</span>
                    <span class="badge role-badge role-fhir">Legacy FHIR</span>
                    <span class="badge role-badge role-application">Application</span>
                    <span class="badge role-badge role-middleware">Middleware</span>
                    <span class="badge role-badge role-security">Security</span>
                    <span class="badge role-badge role-addon">Add-on</span>
                    <span class="badge role-badge role-unknown">Unknown role</span>
                </div>
                        </details>
                        <p>Advanced reader and cache state: open Tools → Viewer diagnostics.</p>
                    </section>
                    <section id="workbench-panel-columns" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="workbench-tab-columns" data-panel="columns" class="workbench-section" hidden><h2>Columns / Display</h2>
                        <p>Choose table columns. Message stays visible to identify and select events. These choices change display only.</p>
                        <fieldset class="column-options"><legend>Visible columns</legend>
<label><input type="checkbox" data-column-toggle="time" data-help-key="logs.columns" onchange="changeColumns('time', this.checked)">Time</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" data-column-toggle="component" data-help-key="logs.columns" onchange="changeColumns('component', this.checked)">Component</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" data-column-toggle="correlationId" data-help-key="logs.columns" onchange="changeColumns('correlationId', this.checked)">Correlation ID</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" data-column-toggle="flowId" data-help-key="logs.columns" onchange="changeColumns('flowId', this.checked)">Flow ID</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" data-column-toggle="traceId" data-help-key="logs.columns" onchange="changeColumns('traceId', this.checked)">Trace ID</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" data-column-toggle="kind" data-help-key="logs.columns" onchange="changeColumns('kind', this.checked)">Type (request / response / processing / other)</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" data-column-toggle="level" data-help-key="logs.columns" onchange="changeColumns('level', this.checked)">Level</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" data-column-toggle="class" data-help-key="logs.columns" onchange="changeColumns('class', this.checked)">Class</label>
<label><input type="checkbox" data-column-toggle="message" data-help-key="logs.column-required" onchange="changeColumns('message', this.checked)" disabled checked>Message (required)</label>
                        </fieldset>
                        <button type="button" class="btn" data-help-key="logs.columns-reset" onclick="changeColumns(null)">Reset to defaults</button>
                        <p id="column-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Display preferences stay in this browser; no event values are saved.</p>
                    </section>
                    <section id="workbench-panel-tools" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="workbench-tab-tools" data-panel="tools" class="workbench-section" hidden><h2>Annotations and export</h2>
                        <details id="viewer-diagnostics"><summary data-help-key="logs.viewer-diagnostics">Viewer diagnostics (advanced)</summary>
                            <p>This describes the viewer, separately from the Diagnostics event-visibility switch in Filters.</p>
                            <p id="log-status" tabindex="0" data-help-key="logs.page-status">Loading bounded log page…</p>
                            <p id="viewer-budgets"></p><p id="viewer-state"></p>
                            <p>Live checks run every 3 seconds. Catch-up keeps the same row/read limits. Offscreen pages at the opposite end are evicted and reload automatically within the captured snapshot. Ordering/grouping apply within each fetched page. Selected details and protected reading anchors remain held; a blocked eviction can defer another page.</p>
                        </details>
                        <p>Diagnostics changes display only. Native detail collection is a private, time-limited service setting; this viewer cannot enable it.</p>
